00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it was the first visit by an iranian  president qatar in a decade  ibrahim raisi's arrival to doha on  monday was also his first trip to a gulf  country since becoming president  whilst doha and tehran have strengthened  their bilateral relations in recent  years iran has found itself  diplomatically and even militarily at  odds with other gulf countries  particularly saudi arabia and the united  arab emirates but in a sign of a  possible shift in regional diplomacy  president raisi stressed his keenness to  improve ties with other gulf corporation  council members  the united states should prove its will  to lift sanctions in order to achieve an  agreement for the nation's benefit  guarantees and closing down of all  political dossiers are of vital  importance our region has entered a new  era after decades of the presence of  occupying forces the region is going  back to its original owners  a number of bilateral deals and  agreements were signed during the visit  but most significant was the messaging  from both leaders qatar's emir  clearly his country's interest in the  restoration of the iranian nuclear deal  we have been briefed regarding the  vienna talks on the agreements between  iran and the west and this matter is  quite important and has a lot of impact  on the stability of the region qatar is  following the negotiations with lot of  interest and we hope that very soon an  agreement could be reached it will  benefit all parties by guaranteeing  rights of all countries to use nuclear  power according to international laws  and agreements  among the other topics discussed by the  two leaders was the developments in  afghanistan with both men highlighting  the need for an inclusive government  there  palestine too is where iran and qatar  find the shared interest  the palestinian cause was also discussed  it is the central issue of our region we  stressed on the immediate need of ending  israeli attacks on the palestinian  people we talked about sorting out the  matter according to international law so  that palestinians are treated fairly and  they can live in stability qatari  diplomacy has witnessed a number of  major successes in recent months  furthering the country's brand as a  mediator and key force in conflict  resolution  whilst iran currently finds itself  embroiled in a number of diplomatic and  military conflicts of its own  from the war in yemen to the standoff  over its nuclear programme the hope is  that stronger qatari iranian relations  will help resolve at least one of those  conflicts  jamal shayal al-jazeera

